.TH TUI_CALCULATOR 1 "2026-07" "v0.1.0" "TUI Calculator Manual"

.SH NAME
tui_calculator \- an advanced CASIO-inspired scientific TUI calculator

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tui_calculator
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIEXPRESSION\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tui_calculator
is a terminal-based scientific calculator built in Rust using Ratatui and
Crossterm. It features 2D math layout rendering (stacked fractions, square
roots, matrix blocks), LaTeX expression syntax, 4-way viewport scrolling,
a responsive layout engine, matrix/vector algebra via nalgebra, and a
non-interactive CLI mode suitable for scripting.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-small
Force the Small layout mode regardless of terminal size.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-medium
Force the Medium layout mode regardless of terminal size.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-big
Force the Big (full) layout mode regardless of terminal size.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.

.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
When an
.I EXPRESSION
argument is provided, the calculator evaluates it and prints the result to
.B stdout
without launching the TUI, then exits with code
.B 0
on success or
.B 1
on error.

.PP
Examples:
.RS
.nf
tui_calculator "sin(30deg) + pi"
tui_calculator "det([[1,2],[3,4]])"
tui_calculator "\\\\frac{1}{2} + \\\\sqrt{9}"
.fi
.RE

.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B Enter / =
Evaluate the current expression.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete the character or token before the cursor.
.TP
.B Arrow Keys
Move cursor left/right; navigate up/down inside fractions or multiline expressions.
.TP
.B Home / End
Jump to the start or end of the expression.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C / q
Quit the application.
.TP
.B ? / F1
Open the interactive help modal (keyboard shortcuts and LaTeX reference).
.TP
.B Tab
Toggle between DEG and RAD angle mode.
.TP
.B Shift+A \[en] Shift+F
Store the current result (ans) into variable A through F.
.TP
.B A \[en] F
Insert the value of variable A through F into the expression.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tui_calculator/config.toml
User configuration file in TOML format. Supported keys:
.RS
.TP
.B angle_unit
\[dq]deg\[dq] or \[dq]rad\[dq] (default: \[dq]deg\[dq])
.TP
.B precision
Number of decimal places to display (default: 6)
.TP
.B default_layout
\[dq]auto\[dq], \[dq]big\[dq], \[dq]medium\[dq], or \[dq]small\[dq] (default: \[dq]auto\[dq])
.TP
.B theme
\[dq]dark\[dq], \[dq]light\[dq], \[dq]dracula\[dq], or \[dq]monokai\[dq] (default: \[dq]dark\[dq])
.TP
.B latex_rendering
true or false (default: true)
.RE

.SH SUPPORTED FUNCTIONS
Trigonometric:
.BR sin ", " cos ", " tan ", " asin ", " acos ", " atan
.PP
Hyperbolic:
.BR sinh ", " cosh ", " tanh
.PP
Logarithmic:
.BR ln ", " log10 ", " log2
.PP
Other:
.BR sqrt ", " abs ", " root(n,x) ", " nCr ", " nPr
.PP
Matrix / Vector:
.BR det ", " inv ", " eigenval ", " eigenvec ", " dot ", " cross ", " norm
.PP
Constants:
.BR pi ", " e

.SH LATEX SYNTAX
The following LaTeX commands are accepted in both TUI and non-interactive mode:
.RS
.nf
\\\\frac{num}{den}
\\\\sqrt{x}
\\\\sin, \\\\cos, \\\\tan, \\\\arcsin, \\\\arccos, \\\\arctan
\\\\det, \\\\vec{v}
\\\\begin{matrix} 1 & 2 \\\\\\\\ 3 & 4 \\\\end{matrix}
\\\\begin{bmatrix} ... \\\\end{bmatrix}
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (non-interactive mode only).
.TP
.B 1
Parse or evaluation error (non-interactive mode only).

